title: Sophos Firewall: High availability
agents: snmp
catalog: hw/network/sophos
license: GPLv2
distribution: https://github.com/KeksDipp/checkmk-plugins
description:
 HA state of a Sophos Firewall cluster: state of this device and of the peer,
 the active node (primary), HA mode and HA link.

 {OK}: both nodes are primary/auxiliary. {CRIT}: a node is faulty,
 standalone or not applicable, both nodes report the same role, there is no
 primary, or HA has been disabled. {WARN}: a node reports "ready"
 (configurable).

 The serial number and role of the monitored address are stored at discovery.
 If they change, a failover has happened and the service goes {WARN}
 (configurable) until it is rediscovered.

discovery:
 One service is created if HA is enabled.
